; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Nautilus Shell
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     logarithmic spiral, exponential, polar coordinates, filled
; SUMMARY:  Draws a logarithmic spiral and divides it into growing chambers, like the shell of a nautilus.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   In a logarithmic spiral the distance from the center is
;   MULTIPLIED by the same amount for every degree turned, instead of
;   having the same amount added. That makes every part of the spiral
;   a scaled-up copy of the part before, which is how a nautilus
;   grows its shell. The program paints the shell turn by turn, then
;   draws the walls between its chambers.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change GROWTH to open the shell up or wind it tighter.
;   Change CHAMBER for more or fewer chamber walls.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * POWER and EXP for growth that multiplies
;   * the formula r = a x growth ^ angle
;   * "self-similar": zoom in on the middle and it looks the same
;   * filling the space between two curves
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make GROWTH 1.002. Does it still look like a shell?
;   * Find the GROWTH where each turn is exactly twice the last
;     (growth ^ 360 = 2).
;   * Draw two spirals going opposite ways, like the seeds in a pine cone.
; ============================================================

make "growth 1.0036        ; r is multiplied by this for each degree
make "start 4.5           ; r at angle 0
make "chamber 24          ; degrees between chamber walls
make "turns 3.1
make "center [0 -50]

to radius :angle
  output :start * power :growth :angle
end

; The point on the spiral at :angle (turtle style: 0 is up, clockwise).
to spot :angle
  localmake "r radius :angle
  output list (first :center) + :r * sin :angle (last :center) + :r * cos :angle
end

; Paint the band between angle a1 and a2 on this turn and the same
; angles one turn further in. Its outline: out along the outer curve,
; back along the inner curve.
to band :a1 :a2 :color
  penup setpos spot :a1
  filled :color [
    for [a :a1 :a2 2] [setpos spot :a]
    for [a :a2 :a1 -2] [setpos spot :a - 360]
  ]
end

; A chamber wall: from a point on the outer turn straight to the
; point at the same angle one turn in.
to wall :a
  penup setpos spot :a
  pendown setpos spot :a - 360
end

to nautilus
  localmake "final 360 * :turns
  ; paint the chambers from the outside in, then draw the walls and
  ; the outline on top of the paint
  for [a :final 360 + :chamber minus :chamber] [
    localmake "t :a / :final
    band :a - :chamber :a (list 250 - 40 * :t 220 - 110 * :t 190 - 150 * :t)
  ]
  setpencolor [120 60 30] setpensize 2
  for [a 360 :final :chamber] [wall :a]
  ; the outline: the whole spiral, thick
  setpensize 4
  penup setpos spot 0
  pendown
  for [a 0 :final 2] [setpos spot :a]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [225 240 245]
nautilus
